1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:01,845
It works on my machine.

2
00:00:01,845 --> 00:00:03,892
Every team has heard that sentence,

3
00:00:03,892 --> 00:00:05,705
and every team has paid for it.

4
00:00:06,255 --> 00:00:10,479
Jenkins fixes it with one rule: the build runs somewhere neutral,

5
00:00:10,479 --> 00:00:11,779
from the repository,

6
00:00:11,779 --> 00:00:13,338
the same way every time.

7
00:00:13,888 --> 00:00:14,285
Today,

8
00:00:14,285 --> 00:00:18,060
Jenkins builds and tests the real CloudCart application,

9
00:00:18,060 --> 00:00:18,789
with Maven,

10
00:00:18,789 --> 00:00:21,504
and shows you the test results as charts.

11
00:00:22,054 --> 00:00:23,804
You will see a build go green,

12
00:00:23,804 --> 00:00:25,087
then break on purpose,

13
00:00:25,087 --> 00:00:25,962
then get fixed.

14
00:00:25,962 --> 00:00:28,411
And you will learn how to read every step.

15
00:00:29,961 --> 00:00:31,390
Here is what to expect.

16
00:00:31,940 --> 00:00:34,820
One: how a change travels from a commit to a result.

17
00:00:35,370 --> 00:00:39,594
Two: the Jenkinsfile that lives inside the CloudCart repository.

18
00:00:40,144 --> 00:00:41,504
Three: a live build.

19
00:00:41,504 --> 00:00:43,611
We tell Jenkins where Maven is,

20
00:00:43,611 --> 00:00:44,630
create the job,

21
00:00:44,630 --> 00:00:45,038
build,

22
00:00:45,038 --> 00:00:46,057
read the tests,

23
00:00:46,057 --> 00:00:47,824
and download the war file.

24
00:00:48,374 --> 00:00:53,174
Four: a way to read a red build, in the right order, and five mistakes to avoid.

25
00:00:53,724 --> 00:00:56,519
This is objective four of the Jenkins domain.

26
00:00:58,569 --> 00:00:59,977
The journey of one change.

27
00:01:00,527 --> 00:01:03,130
A developer pushes a commit to the repository.

28
00:01:03,680 --> 00:01:07,605
Jenkins checks out the code, and reads the Jenkinsfile inside it.

29
00:01:08,155 --> 00:01:10,950
Maven compiles the code, then runs the tests.

30
00:01:11,500 --> 00:01:16,705
Jenkins collects the test results, so you get numbers and charts, not only a long log.

31
00:01:17,255 --> 00:01:19,539
Maven packages the web application,

32
00:01:19,539 --> 00:01:20,388
the war file,

33
00:01:20,388 --> 00:01:23,847
and Jenkins keeps it as an artifact you can download.

34
00:01:24,397 --> 00:01:28,962
If any step fails, the pipeline stops, and the red stage tells you where to look.

35
00:01:30,512 --> 00:01:34,011
Here is the Jenkinsfile in the CloudCart repository.

36
00:01:34,561 --> 00:01:34,943
Tools,

37
00:01:34,943 --> 00:01:39,207
maven: this names the Maven that Jenkins knows from its tools page,

38
00:01:39,207 --> 00:01:42,198
and puts it on the path for the whole pipeline.

39
00:01:42,748 --> 00:01:46,908
Three stages: Build, Test and Package. Names that tell the story.

40
00:01:47,458 --> 00:01:50,338
Build compiles the code. Test runs the tests.

41
00:01:50,888 --> 00:01:51,681
Under Test,

42
00:01:51,681 --> 00:01:52,547
post always,

43
00:01:52,547 --> 00:01:53,052
JUnit.

44
00:01:53,052 --> 00:01:56,298
This reads the report files that Maven wrote,

45
00:01:56,298 --> 00:01:58,462
and gives Jenkins the results,

46
00:01:58,462 --> 00:01:59,400
pass or fail.

47
00:01:59,950 --> 00:02:01,383
Package builds the war,

48
00:02:01,383 --> 00:02:03,314
and archive artifacts keeps it,

49
00:02:03,314 --> 00:02:06,179
so anyone can download exactly what was built.

50
00:02:06,729 --> 00:02:12,617
The dash B flag makes Maven print clean batch logs. That is what you want inside Jenkins.

51
00:02:14,167 --> 00:02:15,280
A real Jenkins,

52
00:02:15,280 --> 00:02:17,656
and the real CloudCart project,

53
00:02:17,656 --> 00:02:18,918
in one recording.

54
00:02:18,918 --> 00:02:20,328
I sign in as admin.

55
00:02:20,328 --> 00:02:20,774
First,

56
00:02:20,774 --> 00:02:23,298
Jenkins needs to know about Maven.

57
00:02:23,848 --> 00:02:24,952
Manage Jenkins,

58
00:02:24,952 --> 00:02:25,910
then Plugins,

59
00:02:25,910 --> 00:02:27,603
then Installed plugins.

60
00:02:27,603 --> 00:02:30,328
Scroll to the M's: Maven Integration.

61
00:02:30,328 --> 00:02:33,789
This plugin is what gives Jenkins a Maven tool.

62
00:02:41,339 --> 00:02:42,965
Back to Manage Jenkins,

63
00:02:42,965 --> 00:02:43,743
then Tools.

64
00:02:43,743 --> 00:02:46,218
Scroll down to Maven installations,

65
00:02:46,218 --> 00:02:47,633
and click Add Maven.

66
00:02:47,633 --> 00:02:49,542
I name it maven three nine.

67
00:02:49,542 --> 00:02:51,734
This machine already has Maven,

68
00:02:51,734 --> 00:02:54,139
so I untick install automatically,

69
00:02:54,139 --> 00:02:55,907
and give its home folder.

70
00:02:55,907 --> 00:02:56,614
Then Save.

71
00:03:03,164 --> 00:03:08,945
Now the job. New Item. The name: CloudCart build. The type: Pipeline. Click OK.

72
00:03:09,495 --> 00:03:11,242
In the Pipeline section,

73
00:03:11,242 --> 00:03:15,174
I change the definition to Pipeline script from SCM.

74
00:03:15,174 --> 00:03:18,669
That says: the pipeline lives in the repository.

75
00:03:18,669 --> 00:03:19,470
SCM: Git.

76
00:03:19,470 --> 00:03:23,037
The repository U R L is a folder on this machine.

77
00:03:23,037 --> 00:03:25,367
At work it is a git hub address.

78
00:03:25,367 --> 00:03:26,750
The branch is main,

79
00:03:26,750 --> 00:03:29,590
and the script path stays Jenkinsfile.

80
00:03:29,590 --> 00:03:29,954
Save.

81
00:03:38,504 --> 00:03:39,144
Build Now.

82
00:03:39,144 --> 00:03:41,256
This first build is the slow one.

83
00:03:41,256 --> 00:03:45,352
Maven downloads everything the project needs from Maven Central.

84
00:03:45,902 --> 00:03:48,707
While we wait: Jenkins checked out the code,

85
00:03:48,707 --> 00:03:50,811
and found the Jenkinsfile in it.

86
00:03:50,811 --> 00:03:53,871
That is why this job needs no script of its own.

87
00:03:53,871 --> 00:03:54,955
When it finishes,

88
00:03:54,955 --> 00:03:56,358
the stages turn green,

89
00:03:56,358 --> 00:03:57,059
one by one.

90
00:04:13,609 --> 00:04:13,938
Done,

91
00:04:13,938 --> 00:04:14,597
and green.

92
00:04:14,597 --> 00:04:15,717
I open the build,

93
00:04:15,717 --> 00:04:17,562
and click Pipeline Overview.

94
00:04:17,562 --> 00:04:17,957
Build,

95
00:04:17,957 --> 00:04:19,077
Test and Package,

96
00:04:19,077 --> 00:04:20,329
each with its time.

97
00:04:25,879 --> 00:04:27,034
Now Test Result.

98
00:04:27,034 --> 00:04:28,261
Thirty two tests,

99
00:04:28,261 --> 00:04:29,128
none failed,

100
00:04:29,128 --> 00:04:30,283
listed by class.

101
00:04:30,283 --> 00:04:34,903
This page exists because of the JUnit line in the Jenkinsfile.

102
00:04:44,453 --> 00:04:45,797
Back on the job page.

103
00:04:45,797 --> 00:04:47,717
Under artifacts: the war file.

104
00:04:47,717 --> 00:04:49,317
That is the build output,

105
00:04:49,317 --> 00:04:51,493
ready to deploy in a later lesson.

106
00:04:52,043 --> 00:04:53,541
Now a real-life moment.

107
00:04:53,541 --> 00:04:56,731
A developer pushes a change to the shipping rule.

108
00:04:56,731 --> 00:04:58,294
I click Build Now again.

109
00:05:12,844 --> 00:05:13,111
Red.

110
00:05:13,111 --> 00:05:14,581
The Test stage failed,

111
00:05:14,581 --> 00:05:16,051
and Package never ran.

112
00:05:16,051 --> 00:05:17,187
I open the build.

113
00:05:17,187 --> 00:05:19,526
Changes shows the commit behind it,

114
00:05:19,526 --> 00:05:21,398
with its author and message.

115
00:05:21,398 --> 00:05:25,808
Test Result shows one failed test: free shipping at the threshold.

116
00:05:25,808 --> 00:05:26,476
Red stage,

117
00:05:26,476 --> 00:05:27,278
test result,

118
00:05:27,278 --> 00:05:27,746
commit.

119
00:05:27,746 --> 00:05:29,484
That is the fastest route.

120
00:05:32,034 --> 00:05:34,679
The developer fixes the rule, and we build again.

121
00:05:41,229 --> 00:05:42,008
Green again.

122
00:05:42,008 --> 00:05:43,048
On the job page,

123
00:05:43,048 --> 00:05:44,996
look at the Test Result Trend.

124
00:05:44,996 --> 00:05:45,776
One red bar,

125
00:05:45,776 --> 00:05:47,010
between green ones.

126
00:05:47,010 --> 00:05:49,933
That is the health of your project over time.

127
00:05:53,483 --> 00:05:58,432
A real build, a real failure, and a real fix. That is Maven in Jenkins.

128
00:05:59,982 --> 00:06:01,774
How to read a red build, in order.

129
00:06:02,324 --> 00:06:07,401
One: which stage is red? That tells you the kind of problem: build, test or package.

130
00:06:07,951 --> 00:06:11,258
Two: Changes. Who changed what since the last green build?

131
00:06:11,808 --> 00:06:16,779
Three: Test Result. Which test failed, and why? Look at expected, against actual.

132
00:06:17,329 --> 00:06:21,659
Four: Console Output, only for the full detail. Start from the bottom.

133
00:06:22,209 --> 00:06:25,708
Five: fix, push, build. Watch the trend go green again.

134
00:06:27,258 --> 00:06:29,647
Five mistakes with Maven in Jenkins.

135
00:06:30,197 --> 00:06:32,509
One: the tool is not configured.

136
00:06:32,509 --> 00:06:33,953
The error says: mvn,

137
00:06:33,953 --> 00:06:35,253
command not found.

138
00:06:35,253 --> 00:06:36,770
Check Manage Jenkins,

139
00:06:36,770 --> 00:06:37,203
Tools,

140
00:06:37,203 --> 00:06:41,248
and make sure the name matches the Jenkinsfile exactly.

141
00:06:41,798 --> 00:06:46,854
Two: no JUnit line. The build is green or red, but there are no test charts.

142
00:06:47,404 --> 00:06:52,311
Three: skipping tests to go faster. A green build that tested nothing is a lie.

143
00:06:52,861 --> 00:06:54,191
Four: no Maven cache.

144
00:06:54,191 --> 00:06:56,662
Every build downloads everything again,

145
00:06:56,662 --> 00:06:57,423
and is slow.

146
00:06:57,423 --> 00:06:59,197
Keep a cache between builds.

147
00:06:59,747 --> 00:07:02,978
Five: editing the job instead of the Jenkinsfile.

148
00:07:02,978 --> 00:07:05,498
The pipeline belongs in the repository,

149
00:07:05,498 --> 00:07:06,403
with the code.

150
00:07:07,953 --> 00:07:10,748
Where to find the lab. Pause here, and write it down.

151
00:07:11,298 --> 00:07:12,762
One: the repository,

152
00:07:12,762 --> 00:07:17,082
git hub dot com slash it dash waves slash dev ops dash A I,

153
00:07:17,082 --> 00:07:19,426
in the folder academy slash lab.

154
00:07:19,976 --> 00:07:26,205
Two: the files, lab157 dot sh, and shortcuts one fifty-seven dot sh.

155
00:07:26,755 --> 00:07:32,216
Three: install it, with sudo install, into slash user slash local slash S bin.

156
00:07:32,766 --> 00:07:34,624
Four: load the short names,

157
00:07:34,624 --> 00:07:37,788
with source shortcuts one fifty-seven dot sh.

158
00:07:37,788 --> 00:07:38,613
Then lab up,

159
00:07:38,613 --> 00:07:39,508
and lab repo.

160
00:07:40,058 --> 00:07:43,962
Five: lab bad makes the broken commit. Lab fix repairs it.

161
00:07:44,512 --> 00:07:48,291
Six: you need the Jenkins from lesson one fifty-five,

162
00:07:48,291 --> 00:07:49,004
plus Java,

163
00:07:49,004 --> 00:07:50,002
Maven and git.

164
00:07:50,002 --> 00:07:52,213
Lab down removes the lab files.

165
00:07:52,763 --> 00:07:54,406
The link is in the description.

166
00:07:56,456 --> 00:07:58,227
Your turn, on your own machine.

167
00:07:58,777 --> 00:08:02,595
One: lab up, then lab repo, and read the Jenkinsfile it made.

168
00:08:03,145 --> 00:08:06,815
Two: add the Maven tool, and create the job from SCM.

169
00:08:07,365 --> 00:08:10,650
Three: build it, and open Test Result and the war file.

170
00:08:11,200 --> 00:08:14,016
Four: lab bad, build, and find the failed test.

171
00:08:14,566 --> 00:08:17,169
Five: lab fix, build, and look at the trend.

172
00:08:17,719 --> 00:08:19,553
Pause the video, and begin now.

173
00:08:35,103 --> 00:08:35,978
Quick check.

174
00:08:36,528 --> 00:08:38,917
Which line gives Jenkins the Maven tool?

175
00:08:39,467 --> 00:08:41,856
Which line gives you test results and charts?

176
00:08:42,406 --> 00:08:44,646
What is the fastest route through a red build?

177
00:08:45,196 --> 00:08:47,543
Why is a build with skipped tests dangerous?

178
00:08:48,093 --> 00:08:50,529
Objective covered: MC17,

179
00:08:50,529 --> 00:08:51,637
objective four.

180
00:08:51,637 --> 00:08:55,624
Building and testing CloudCart with Maven in Jenkins.

181
00:08:56,174 --> 00:08:58,243
Pause the video, and answer out loud.

